    "description": "Anza provides a software-enabled marketplace and analytics platform used by solar and storage developers, independent power producers, and corporate energy buyers to source equipment. Its operating model is asset-light relative to power generation platforms, with revenues tied to subscription, transaction support, and procurement services rather than ownership of operating plants. The business focuses on helping customers evaluate module, inverter, and storage options using market data and comparative analytics. The company states that it was formally launched in 2022 and completed its separation from Borrego in 2023 with new backing from an Energy Capital Partners-led consortium that included Angeleno Group. Anza reported in early 2026 that its platform had supported more than 2 GW of solar safe-harbor procurements during 2025 and more than 9.2 GW of solar purchase orders over the prior five years.",
